  body: "# Income Support prisoner applicable amount\n\nCaptured DMG 24212 gives a nil applicable amount
    for the sentenced-prisoner branch of 24197(1) and explicitly says a claimant with a nil applicable
    amount is not entitled. DMG 24214 allows possible remand entitlement with allowable housing costs,
    otherwise nil. Definitions, detention dates, hospital legislation and partner treatment must be read
    separately; prisoner here includes a sentence by a criminal, civil or military court.\n\n## Scope
    and limitations\n\nFrozen DMG research: listed legacy JSA(Cont), JSA(IB), IS, SPC and ESA(Cont)/ESA(IR)
    imprisonment guidance captured on 15 September 2026. This is an explanation of the captured text,
    not a determination of contemporary individual eligibility.\n\nIndependent experimental research,
    not an official DWP document, benefits advice, a calculation or an individual entitlement decision.
    All authored meanings and dependencies require specialist review.\n\nThe broad labels JSA and ESA
    do not establish a claimant’s regime. This profile explains the listed DMG legacy regimes; New Style
    JSA/ESA, UC and PIP are routed to ADM by 12016. Those ADM bodies are not acquired. Ask for regime/date
    and fresh authoritative checks before applying guidance to a person.\n\nThe payability statement at
    12003 is scoped by the list in 12002. It cannot replace benefit-specific rules or establish that entitlement
    always survives imprisonment.\n\nMachine-extracted whole pages retain neighbouring text, partial unrelated
    paragraphs, footnotes, historical examples and possible reading-order errors. Use the stated locators;
    page presence is not full legal interpretation or PDF visual review.\n\nCapture date is not publication,
    revision or commencement. Old amendment footers and example dates remain literal source text. The
    currently linked catalogue is not current-law assurance; legislation and case law have not been consolidated
    or reconciled.\n\nThe frozen PDFs still refer to Memo 07/20. Official catalogue history says it was
    removed because the regulations ceased to have effect from 31 August 2021. The memo body is absent;
    do not revive that temporary exception.\n\n12016’s ADM M1 reference conflicts with the frozen catalogue
    title marking M1 spare. S1/U6 are identified routes, not acquired evidence. Internal Chapter 41 references
    to 53112 and 53071 and the printed Chapter 53 number 531261 remain unresolved version/typographic
    observations.\n\nPrisoner definitions differ by benefit: do not transfer the general criminal/civil
    distinction indiscriminately. Remand, bail hostel, sentence, release, hospital legislation, fine default,
    overseas detention, time limits and partner circumstances require the relevant branch. Housing-cost
    passages do not establish a current housing award."
